http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.hack/msg/ca4a8b4448f4acff, posted 10
December 1992, announced the release of "NetHack++".  This variant, quickly
renamed NetHack-- to avoid silly questions about a C++ rewrite, is the earliest
ancestor of SLASH'EM that is not a vanilla NH release.

Fifteen years ago last December 10.

The then-current version of NetHack was 3.0.10, and it was a very different
game. The dungeon was still strictly linear, and still used the Hack lighting
model: corridors were dark, and a room was entirely either dark or lit. Shaped
keys were still around. Hell began after the Castle, and fire resistance was
necessary to enter.

